EU ministers meeting in the General  Affairs Council looked at the draft  agenda of the next European Council in  October and agreed that they are getting  closer to consensus on a final decision  about a new climate and energy policy  framework we have globally detected a  desire and a determination by all  participating member states in this  discussion to to come to an agreement at  the European Council on the new energy  climate framework but at the same time  we've also noted that there are still  many issues that need to be further  explored in order to find suitable and  acceptable compromises at the next  summit EU leaders are also expected to  discuss the economic situation in Europe  as well as international developments on  the basis of a report prepared by the  Italian presidency ministers also looked  at how to accelerate the implementation  of measures aimed at fostering growth  jobs and competitiveness in Europe  finally ministers adopted conclusions on  the EU strategy for the adriatic and a  union region this strategy aims at  strengthening cooperation between the  eight participating countries to the  benefit of 70 million citizens in the  light of the positive experience held in  the Baltic and in the linear region we  are confident than that this strategy  which will have to be endorsed by the  European Council in October we we  provide a very effective tool notably at  regional level for the better  implementation and promotion of you  common common strategy the idea is to  work together to tackle challenges which  are common to all countries in the  region so just protecting the marine  environment completing the transport and  energy networks and promoting  sustainable tourism
 

